mdhn:Story_of_Salih_and_the_She_Camel a mdhn:NarrativeEpisode ;
    rdfs:label "Ṣāliḥ and the She-Camel from the Mountain"@en ,
               "صالح و ناقه از کوه"@fa ,
               "Salih produces the she-camel from the rock"@en ;    
    rdfs:comment """The Arab prophet Ṣāliḥ (Salih) leads or brings forth the miraculous 
    she-camel (nāqat Allāh) from the side of a mountain / rock. 
    The people of Thamūd demanded a sign of his prophethood; God caused a she-camel 
    to emerge from the rock as a test and a blessing. 
    The scene is a standard subject in Qiṣaṣ al-Anbiyāʾ and appears in the 
    Jāmiʿ al-Tawārīkh of Rashīd al-Dīn."""@en ;    
    mdhn:icWikiDataURL "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q326189" ;      
    mdhn:charactersInvolved mdhn:Salih, mdhn:Camel_of_Salih;    
    mdhn:isPartOf mdhn:Islamic_Mythology, mdhn:Qisas_al_Anbiya ;    
    skos:exactMatch   mdhn:iconclass_Salih_SheCamel ;
    skos:relatedMatch wd:Q326189 .    

mdhn:Qisas_al_Anbiya a mdhn:NarrativeEpisode ;
    mdhn:aatConcept mdhn:aat300404209 ;
    mdhn:icWikiDataURL "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1087563" ;
    mdhn:isPartOf  mdhn:Islamic_Mythology ;
    rdfs:comment """The Qiṣaṣ al-anbiyā (Arabic: قِصَص الْأَنـۢبِيَاء, lit. 'Stories of the Prophets') is any of various collections of stories about figures recognised as prophets and messengers in Islam, closely related to tafsīr (exegesis of the Qur'an)."""@en ;
    rdfs:label "Qisas al-Anbiya"@en , "قِصَص الْأَنـۢبِيَاء"@fa . 

