mdhn:Golestan_of_Saadi a mdhn:NarrativeEpisode ;
    mdhn:aatConcept mdhn:aat300404746 ;
    mdhn:icWikiDataURL "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q404191" ;
    dcterms:created "656 AH / 1258 CE" ;
    mdhn:isPartOf mdhn:Folklore_Epic_or_Mythology ;
    mdhn:charactersInvolved mdhn:Saadi_Shirazi ;
    rdfs:comment """The Golestan (Gulistan, 'Rose Garden') is the prose-and-verse masterpiece of Saadi of Shiraz, completed in 656/1258 and dedicated to the Salghurid Atabeg of Fars. After a preface it is arranged in eight chapters (bab), likened by the author to the eight gates of paradise. Each bab gathers independent hikayat (anecdotes) interspersed with short poems. The work is one of the most frequently copied and illustrated books of Persian literature."""@en ;
    rdfs:label "Golestan of Saadi"@en , "گلستان سعدی"@fa .


### Preface (دیباچه)

mdhn:Golestan_Preface a mdhn:NarrativeEpisode ;
    rdfs:label "Preface of the Golestan"@en , "دیباچه گلستان"@fa ;
    rdfs:comment """Opening of the Golestan: praise of God, panegyric of the Atabeg of Fars, and Saadi's account of why he composed a 'rose garden' whose leaves autumn cannot wither."""@en ;
    mdhn:charactersInvolved mdhn:Saadi_Shirazi ;
    mdhn:isPartOf mdhn:Golestan_of_Saadi ;
    mdhn:icWikiDataURL "" .

mdhn:Cause_of_Composing_Golestan a mdhn:NarrativeEpisode ;
    rdfs:label "The Cause of Composing the Rose Garden"@en , "سبب تصنیف گلستان"@fa ;
    rdfs:comment """In the preface Saadi, walking with a friend, gathers roses; the friend asks for a book whose pages will not fade. Saadi undertakes the Golestan."""@en ;
    mdhn:charactersInvolved mdhn:Saadi_Shirazi ;
    mdhn:isPartOf mdhn:Golestan_Preface ;
    mdhn:icWikiDataURL "" .

mdhn:Saadi_and_Friend_in_the_Garden a mdhn:NarrativeEpisode ;
    rdfs:label "Saadi converses by night with a young friend in a garden"@en , "گفتگوی شبانه سعدی با دوست در باغ"@fa ;
    rdfs:comment """Canonical illustrated episode of the Golestan preface / garden frame: Saadi sitting with a companion among roses. Famous example: Herat 1427, Chester Beatty Library, workshop of Baysunghur."""@en ;
    mdhn:charactersInvolved mdhn:Saadi_Shirazi ;
    mdhn:isPartOf mdhn:Golestan_Preface ;
    mdhn:icWikiDataURL "" .


### Bab 1 — The Manners of Kings (سیرت پادشاهان)

mdhn:Golestan_Bab_1_Manners_of_Kings a mdhn:NarrativeEpisode ;
    rdfs:label "Golestan Chapter 1: The Manners of Kings"@en , "گلستان باب اول: در سیرت پادشاهان"@fa ;
    rdfs:comment "First bab of the Golestan. Anecdotes on justice, clemency, tyranny and counsel at court (about 41 hikayat)."@en ;
    mdhn:isPartOf mdhn:Golestan_of_Saadi ;
    mdhn:icWikiDataURL "" .

mdhn:Golestan_King_and_the_Prisoner a mdhn:NarrativeEpisode ;
    rdfs:label "The King and the Prisoner"@en , "پادشاه و اسیر"@fa ;
    rdfs:comment """Bab 1, hikayat 1. A padshah orders a prisoner killed; the desperate man curses the king. A vizier interprets the curse as a pious utterance and obtains a pardon — a lesson on clemency."""@en ;
    mdhn:isPartOf mdhn:Golestan_Bab_1_Manners_of_Kings ;
    mdhn:icWikiDataURL "" .

mdhn:Golestan_Slave_and_the_Ship a mdhn:NarrativeEpisode ;
    rdfs:label "The Slave and the Ship"@en , "غلام و کشتی"@fa ;
    rdfs:comment """Bab 1. A king takes slave-boys on a ship; one who has never seen the sea wails in terror. A sage has him thrown overboard briefly so that, once hauled back, he values the ship. Frequently illustrated."""@en ;
    mdhn:isPartOf mdhn:Golestan_Bab_1_Manners_of_Kings ;
    mdhn:icWikiDataURL "" .

mdhn:Golestan_Hajjaj_and_the_Dervish a mdhn:NarrativeEpisode ;
    rdfs:label "Hajjaj and the Dervish"@en , "حجاج و درویش مستجاب‌الدعوه"@fa ;
    rdfs:comment """Bab 1. Hajjaj Yusuf summons a dervish whose prayers are answered and asks for a blessing. The dervish prays that God take Hajjaj's life — 'a blessing for you and for all Muslims'."""@en ;
    mdhn:isPartOf mdhn:Golestan_Bab_1_Manners_of_Kings ;
    mdhn:icWikiDataURL "" .

mdhn:Golestan_Hypocritical_Ascetic_at_Court a mdhn:NarrativeEpisode ;
    rdfs:label "The Hypocritical Ascetic at the King's Table"@en , "زاهد ریاکار مهمان پادشاه"@fa ;
    rdfs:comment """An ascetic eats less than his appetite and prays more than his habit when dining with a king, so that others think him more pious. Source of the couplet 'I fear you will not reach the Ka'ba, O Arab, for the road you take leads to Turkestan'."""@en ;
    mdhn:isPartOf mdhn:Golestan_Bab_1_Manners_of_Kings ;
    mdhn:icWikiDataURL "" .

mdhn:Golestan_Chinese_Slave_Girl a mdhn:NarrativeEpisode ;
    rdfs:label "The King and the Chinese Slave Girl"@en , "ملک و کنیزک چینی"@fa ;
    rdfs:comment """Bab 1, hikayat 40. A king is given a Chinese slave girl; when she refuses him in drunkenness he gives her in anger to an ugly black slave."""@en ;
    mdhn:isPartOf mdhn:Golestan_Bab_1_Manners_of_Kings ;
    mdhn:icWikiDataURL "" .

mdhn:Golestan_Alexander_Asked_About_Conquest a mdhn:NarrativeEpisode ;
    rdfs:label "Alexander Asked How He Conquered East and West"@en , "پرسش از اسکندر رومی در فتح مشرق و مغرب"@fa ;
    rdfs:comment """Bab 1, hikayat 41. Alexander is asked how he conquered the world when earlier kings had more treasure and troops. He answers that he never reviled fallen kings. Closing hikayat of the first bab."""@en ;
    mdhn:charactersInvolved mdhn:Iskandar_Dhul_Qarnayn ;
    mdhn:isPartOf mdhn:Golestan_Bab_1_Manners_of_Kings ;
    mdhn:icWikiDataURL "" .


### Bab 2 — The Morals of Dervishes (اخلاق درویشان)

mdhn:Golestan_Bab_2_Morals_of_Dervishes a mdhn:NarrativeEpisode ;
    rdfs:label "Golestan Chapter 2: The Morals of Dervishes"@en , "گلستان باب دوم: در اخلاق درویشان"@fa ;
